// PARAM: --analysis congruence
// x is 0 (mod 2) whatever n is, so x == 3 is concretely false at every
// execution and (x != 3) is a fixed fact.
//
// The concrete mechanism is congruence_eqb (Congruence_Arithmetic.thy): it
// reads congruence_singleton off both sides and answers only when both
// pin a single integer (modulus 0). Here x has modulus 2, so it declines
// before ever comparing residues -- even though the two classes are
// visibly disjoint. Refuting whenever r1 != r2 (mod gcd m1 m2) is within
// the domain's representation, not beyond it; the implementation just does
// not reach for it.
//
// Two contrasts pin how narrow this gap is. --analysis parity proves the
// same shape, because Even and Odd are disjoint by construction there. And
// Congruence itself refutes exactly this claim when it appears as a guard
// instead of a check (../precision/03-residue_guard_kills_branch.vimp),
// since the guard path goes through intersect_congruence, which does
// compare the classes.
fun main() {
  n = __voblint_nondet_int();
  x = 2 * n;
  __voblint_check(x != 3); // UNKNOWN
}
